============================================================
Pixel scaling / colour conversion
============================================================

This product includes software developed by the LibYuv Project Authors
(libyuv).
  - Source:   https://github.com/lemenkov/libyuv
               (a maintained fork of the original
                chromium.googlesource.com/external/libyuv)
  - Version:  master @ 209763ad77fed3df2d57503d3ef40761e9473649
              (LIBYUV_VERSION 1982; vendored at src/third_party/libyuv/;
               pinned SHA in src/third_party/SOURCE_VERSIONS)
  - License:  BSD-3-Clause
  - Scope:    runtime, statically linked (NIMRTC_VENDORED_LIBYUV=ON, the
              default).  Built from source.  Serves as the SIMD YUV/RGB
              scale + convert backend behind
              `nimrtc::video_frame::VideoFrameScaler` (the remote-desktop
              plan's Track C "Pixel" work item).
  - Platforms (cross-platform vendoring policy K8b):
              Windows (MSVC)  — x86-64, SSSE3 + AVX2
              macOS           — arm64, NEON
              Linux x86-64    — SSSE3 + AVX2
              Linux aarch64   — NEON / SVE2 / SME
              Android         — arm64 / x86, NEON / SSSE3
              iOS             — arm64, NEON
              The library is built from the same source on every platform,
              so the scale output is identical across platforms (the
              plan's "same-result check").  No prebuilt binary is linked
              or shipped.

============================================================
Audio I/O (capture + playback)
============================================================

This product includes software developed by the PortAudio contributors
(PortAudio Portable Real-Time Audio Library).
  - Source:   https://github.com/PortAudio/portaudio
  - Version:  master @ 8b6333ff8744b22afaa694bc4b8b22f6f0dba6dd
              (vendored at src/third_party/portaudio/; pinned SHA in
               src/third_party/SOURCE_VERSIONS)
  - License:  MIT  (the notice is embedded verbatim at the top of
                   every upstream source file; the full text is in
                   src/third_party/portaudio/src/LICENSE.txt)
  - Scope:    runtime, statically linked (NIMRTC_VENDORED_PORTAUDIO=ON,
              the default).  Built from source.  Serves as the audio
              I/O backend behind `nimrtc::audio_device` (the
              remote-desktop plan's Track F "Device" work item) — ONE
              implementation replaces the WASAPI + CoreAudio +
              ALSA/PulseAudio triple that RD-10 forbids hand-writing.
  - Platforms (cross-platform vendoring policy K8b):
              Windows (MSVC)  — x86-64, WASAPI + MME + DirectSound
              macOS           — arm64 / x86-64, Core Audio
              Linux x86-64    — ALSA + PulseAudio (each enabled only
                                when the build host carries the
                                corresponding development package)
              The library is built from the same source on every
              platform.  No system audio library is *required*: without
              any backend the library still compiles and PortAudio
              reports "no host API" at runtime.
  - Note:     ASIO, WDM-KS and JACK are deliberately NOT built — the
              Steinberg ASIO SDK may not be redistributed, and neither
              libjack nor the KS driver is a NimRTC dependency.

